WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.970
It's Cake Week here at the show

2
00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:04.700
and we have someone that we're gonna talk to right now

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.150
and I'm very excited.

4
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.710
Michaela is here and she is

5
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.480
a nurse in the public health circuit

6
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.340
of the COVID-19 response team in Seattle

7
00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.180
and she uses her love of baking

8
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.430
to raise money for racial justice.

9
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.323
Please welcome Michaela Banks.

10
00:00:22.323 --> 00:00:24.610
(audience cheering)
Hi, Michaela.

11
00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:25.738
Oh, wow.

12
00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:26.750
Hi, Drew Barrymore.

13
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:27.583
Hi, Ross.

14
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:28.560
Hi.

15
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.210
So listen, I grew up right up there near Seattle.

16
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.850
So, I'm so inspired by what you're doing.

17
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.030
This is great.

18
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:36.700
Yeah.
Oh, that's great.

19
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:37.970
What inspired you?

20
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.073
You auction off your cakes and please explain.

21
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.300
Yeah, so all of this started,

22
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.980
I love that cakes and sweet treats are so disarming.

23
00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.520
And so, when we talk about racial justice,

24
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.110
it kind of grounds us to this place of seeking justice

25
00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.930 line:15%
for people, seeking rightness for people is sweet.

26
00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.170 line:15%
It's lovely.

27
00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.900 line:15%
And even holding accountable

28
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.890 line:15%
the parts of myself that cause harm,

29
00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.010 line:15%
that's hard, but it's beautiful.

30
00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:09.100
And so, there's this sentiment about Toni Morrison,

31
00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.480
so Dr. Farah Griffin said in "The Pieces I Am" documentary,

32
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.490
Tony Morrison said, "What can I do where I am?"

33
00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:18.570
And so, as I was reflecting on that, I thought,

34
00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.170
one of the things I have to give is a baking habit.

35
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.900
So I started auctioning off my first cake

36
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.690
for Equal Justice Initiative

37
00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.070
and the heart behind all of this, the whole time,

38
00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.070
has been, how can we dive deeper into learning?

39
00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:32.990
What are the issues?

40
00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:33.823
What's going on?

41
00:01:33.823 --> 00:01:36.280
And then, what are people already doing about it?

42
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.880
The work has been happening.

43
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.230
Let's follow in the lead of the heroes

44
00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.930
in the streets and the courtrooms and the classrooms.

45
00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:47.210
And so, enjoy a cake while really giving of ourselves

46
00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.226
to support what's important.

47
00:01:49.226 --> 00:01:50.390
I like that.
Oh, Michaela.

48
00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.600
We love what you are doing
(clapping)

49
00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:56.690
and what you and your cakes represent is so meaningful.

50
00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:59.380
I'm gonna be thinking about that Toni Morrison quote, too.

51
00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.777
Yeah.
"Do what you can

52
00:02:00.777 --> 00:02:01.630
"where you are."

53
00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.340
I will carry that with us in honor

54
00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.300
of your bringing that into a light for us.

55
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.070
And Ross and I would love to bid $5000

56
00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.590
to you and donate it towards the NAACP,

57
00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.950
a charity we understand is very close to your heart.

58
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.154
Yes.
(audience clapping)

59
00:02:18.154 --> 00:02:19.214
Are you for real?

60
00:02:19.214 --> 00:02:20.570
Yeah!

61
00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.210
Keep up that great work.
(clapping)

62
00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:23.610
We applaud you Michaela.

63
00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.830
Thank you for coming on the show and shining a light.

64
00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.940
And obviously, if you go to the DrewBarrymoreShow.com,

65
00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.300
Michaela's work, her website, her Instagram,

66
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.410
everything will be on there

67
00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:34.650
if you would like to join in this as well.

68
00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.550
Thank you, Michaela.

69
00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.133
(upbeat music)

